{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3c9c0718e9969a44f0d98a133ca8a12e443ba89e64b970c4fbaf84c171e1e9c2","digest":{"component_or_area":"test: pinned-view / git object storage","key_entities":["tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py::test_tree_listed_ticket_blob_missing_from_object_database_fails_closed","loose_object","blob_oid","git gc --auto","gc.auto","git pack-objects","src/rebar/_store/sync.py","src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_objects.py","objects/ab/cdef"],"problem_keywords":["test setup precondition failure","flaky test","git object storage","loose vs packed objects","object database","test determinism"],"propositions":["The test precondition fails intermittently on CI when git packs a blob before the test assertion checks for it as a loose object file.","The test was designed to verify pinned-view fails closed on missing ticket blobs, but fails on its own setup assertion before exercising that behavior.","Packing threshold differences between fresh CI stores and developer machines cause the same test code to pass locally but fail on CI.","The test must deterministically handle both object storage shapes (loose and packed) without using threshold-dependent git gc.","Removing a full pack to make objects unreadable is too coarse and causes false passes (missing tree instead of missing target blob)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787910796058279001,"uuid":"dd78af6b-9cea-4f8e-9e64-19312afb1d4d"}